# Line endings are pinned here rather than left to each machine's config.
#
# Git for Windows ships core.autocrlf=true in its SYSTEM config, so without
# this file these sources check out as CRLF. Prettier is configured
# endOfLine:"lf" and `npm run validate` enforces it, so a fresh Windows
# clone would fail the gate on every file it touches — and every `git add`
# prints "LF will be replaced by CRLF the next time Git touches it".
#
# text=auto eol=lf keeps LF in the index AND in the working tree regardless
# of local core.autocrlf, which is what both Prettier and the CI gate want.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Images: never line-ending-converted, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
